message: "If you use this knowledge object, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Two-Factor Prognostic Model for Diabetic Foot Ulcer Healing by 16 Weeks"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
authors:
  - name: "Knowledge Systems Lab"
    affiliation: "Department of Learning Health Sciences, University of Michigan Medical School"
    email: "kgrid-developers@umich.edu"
    website: "https://ror.org/00jmfr291"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kgrid-objects/FAIR-DO-Workshop"
url: "https://github.com/kgrid-objects/FAIR-DO-Workshop/tree/dfu-prognostic-indicator-ko-v1.0.0/collection/DFU-Prognostic-Indicator-KO"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  This knowledge object estimates the model-based probability that one diabetic foot ulcer will heal by 16 weeks, using only wound area and wound duration measured at the first clinical visit. It is a categorical pretreatment prognosis; not a continuous individualized risk equation, treatment-effect estimate, HBOT eligibility decision, or treatment recommendation.
keywords:
  - FAIR Digital Object
